---
description: Preserve Builder behavior during state migration and decomposition
globs: client/src/Builder/**/*.{js,jsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Builder Change Safety

- Preserve current Builder UI, behavior, data contracts, and persistence semantics.
- Keep changes narrow; do not refactor unrelated Builder code during a fix.
- Never remove working logic merely to satisfy lint.
- Before removing unused Context state or actions, confirm Zustand migration and search for all consumers.
- Keep server state as the source of truth; Zustand manages client state and coordinated metadata.
- Partition multisite state by siteId and localized state by locale where required.
- Prevent stale async responses from one site or page updating another.
- Do not add Auto-save unless explicitly requested.

# content.jsx Decomposition

- Decompose incrementally, one responsibility at a time.
- Establish UI and performance baselines before extraction.
- Start with low-coupling utilities; move DnD, Canvas, and performance code only with focused testing.
- Do not split content.jsx merely to reduce line count.
- Preserve refs, event ordering, synchronous commits, drag cleanup, Ghost behavior, and keyboard/focus behavior.
- After each extraction, run lint and production build, then re-test affected interactions.

# Quality Gate

- Do not disable ESLint rules to hide root causes.
- Do not add dependencies without explicit need.
- Do not change Builder Performance Monitor thresholds or measurement behavior.
- Record deferred architectural or bundle work in BUILD_FOLLOWUP_NOTES.txt.
